# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/antigravity-cli/ is
# gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS (Google's Antigravity CLI,
# Gemini 3.x; see `[tool.antigravity-cli]` in currency.toml, which Ray graded a
# CRITICAL currency dependency 2026-08-19). This file existed since 2026-08-02
# (#496) with none of the header its peers (`sources/hk.manifest`,
# `sources/mise.manifest`, `sources/codex.manifest`) carry, which the
# 2026-09-03 cold review of 575fb5be flagged as plausibly why it sat at 1.1.20
# through the 1.1.21/1.1.22/1.1.23 bumps unnoticed. This header is that fix.
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: mise.toml `[tools] antigravity-cli` (`aqua:` backend)
#   pinned here:    1.1.25
# A pin that drifts from the installed version makes the corpus answer
# questions about code we are not running. Not hypothetical —
# `sources/graphify.manifest` records exactly that failure: it sat two
# releases behind for weeks, so every "how does graphify work?" answer came
# from the wrong source.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head — a branch drifts ahead of the
# release. Tags here are LIGHTWEIGHT (confirmed 2026-09-03: zero `^{}` peeled
# lines across all 39 tags), so the plain `git ls-remote --tags <url> <tag>`
# commit is the one to record — the annotated-tag trap in
# `sources/hk.manifest`/`sources/mise.manifest` (#395/#500) does not apply
# here, but re-check it on every bump rather than assuming.
# To bump:
#   git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli <version>
# and set ref/commit here to that line's SHA, then `mise run kb-build`.
#
# kind = docs, NOT code (changed 2026-09-03, cold review of 575fb5be). At the
# pinned commit the repo is 15 blobs and zero source files — the CLI itself
# ships as prebuilt release tarballs, not as source in this tree. `kind = code`
# would extract nothing (its two `.sh` files live under `examples/`, demo
# scripts, not the tool) while silently skipping `CHANGELOG.md` and
# `README.md` by design — the one artifact that lets the corpus answer "what
# changed between 1.1.20 and 1.1.25". `kind = docs` ingests exactly those two
# files instead.
url = https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli
ref = 1.1.25
commit = 7e1316ca775dc3805aac13b2db5cd37d89d5aae8
kind = docs
added = 2026-08-02
